When the MATCH query walks the iterator into page 2, the inner while( pChunk[i] & 0x80 ) runs ~996 times before the buffer ends, then fts5BufferSafeAppendBlob is called with i-iStart of roughly 996 against a 10-byte buffer. In an assert-enabled build this is caught immediately by the buffer's own invariant. In a stripped release build the memcpy corrupts ~986 bytes of adjacent heap.

