Summary
Vuln26 reports that step 6 of sqlite3ExprCodeIN() picks the collation from the LHS expression only (sqlite3ExprCollSeq(pParse, p)) while the KeyInfo at line 3754 uses both sides. This is a second, independent step-6 bug in the same function. When sqlite3FindInIndex() selects an existing index whose column order differs from the SELECT column order, it builds an aiMap[] permutation and the LHS registers rLhs+0, rLhs+1, ... are written in the index's column order, not the original LHS order. Step 6 at src/expr.c:4262-4283 then walks the comparison loop without consulting aiMap:
for(i=0; i<nVector; i++){
Expr *p;
CollSeq *pColl;
int r3 = sqlite3GetTempReg(pParse);
p = sqlite3VectorFieldSubexpr(pLeft, i);                /* line 4265  LHS field i */
if( ExprUseXSelect(pExpr) ){
Expr *pRhs = pExpr->x.pSelect->pEList->a[i].pExpr;    /* RHS field i */
pColl = sqlite3BinaryCompareCollSeq(pParse, p, pRhs);
}else{
pColl = sqlite3ExprCollSeq(pParse, p);
}
sqlite3VdbeAddOp3(v, OP_Column, iTab, i, r3);           /* RHS column i */
sqlite3VdbeAddOp4(v, OP_Ne, rLhs+i, destNotNull, r3,    /* LHS register i */
(void*)pColl, P4_COLLSEQ);
...
}

Both p (used to pick pColl) and rLhs+i (the LHS operand actually compared) are indexed by the loop variable i, but they no longer refer to the same logical column when the index reordered the LHS into the register file. Step 6 ends up comparing the LHS column at index position i against the RHS column at SELECT position i, using the collation of the SELECT-position-i LHS field. With a NOCASE column and a BINARY column swapped by the index, the comparison flips between matching and not matching, and a NULL element in the LHS makes step 6 conclude NULL when the correct answer is FALSE (or vice versa).

The bug needs a vector IN whose RHS is a SELECT ... FROM t, an index on t whose column order is a non-identity permutation of the SELECT order, columns with differing collations, and a NULL element in the LHS to force step 6 to run.

PoC
