Summary
In ext/misc/unionvtab.c, a unionvtab (or swarmvtab) source query returns one row per backing table as (db, table, lo, hi). unionConnect() reads the table name with sqlite3_column_text(pStmt, 1) (line 934) and copies it via unionStrdup() (line 963). unionStrdup(NULL) returns 0 without setting an error (line 276 to 286), so pSrc->zTab becomes NULL and flows unchecked into unionIsIntkeyTable(), which calls sqlite3_table_column_metadata(db, pSrc->zDb, pSrc->zTab, "_rowid_", ...) with a NULL table name (lines 521 to 522). Because this build does not define SQLITE_ENABLE_API_ARMOR, the zTableName==0 guard in main.c is compiled out, so NULL reaches sqlite3FindTable(db, NULL, zDb) and then sqlite3HashFind(&tblHash, NULL), whose strHash() walks while(z[0]) from address 0 (CWE-476). The crafted source query is fully attacker-controlled text, so this is reachable from pure SQL via the loadable unionvtab extension. Impact is a process-level denial of service.

Buildgcc -g -fsanitize=address -fPIC -shared \
-I/data/ylwang/LargeScan/targets/sqlite \
/data/ylwang/LargeScan/targets/sqlite/ext/misc/unionvtab.c \
-o unionvtab.so

(The main sqlite3 binary already links libasan, so the extension is monitored under the real binary's sanitizer.)

PoC
