Fix
Fix up (or invalidate) active backups when collapsing the database array. In sqlite3CollapseDatabaseArray() / the DETACH path, decrement iSrc/iDest of every live backup whose index is above the removed slot, or block the detach when any backup index would be invalidated. For example, extend the in-backup guard to scan all live backups rather than only the db being detached:
/* src/attach.c: detachFunc() — also reject detaching a db below an active
** backup's source/dest, since CollapseDatabaseArray() would shift its index. */
for(pBk = sqlite3PagerBackupPtr(...); pBk; pBk = pBk->pNext){ ... }
/* or, in build.c CollapseDatabaseArray(), adjust b->iSrc/b->iDest for
** every backup on this connection whose index > the collapsed slot. */

Summary
The %!J formatter expands a positive UTF-8 character precision into a byte
count using i64, but later passes the expanded distance to an int append
length. A valid 4 GiB-scale UTF-8 input can therefore narrow to -1 and reach
an oversized memcpy().

Affected Area

SQLite version or Fossil check-in: 3.54.0 / dc4763b14c421710f2a19c19c1cac455c1d0
Build options or relevant feature flags: Default amalgamation build
Component or source path: src/printf.c, sqlite3VXPrintf(), and public
SQLite printf APIs.

Steps to Reproduce
The PoC calls sqlite3_snprintf() with %!.*J, precision 1073741824, and a
NUL-terminated UTF-8 buffer whose encoded byte count is 0xffffffff. ASan
reports a negative-size append reaching memcpy().

