decimalNewFromText() (ext/misc/decimal.c:87) begins with for(i=0; IsSpace(zIn[i]); i++){} with no i<n guard, and collation keys are not NUL-terminated, so an all-whitespace key compared under COLLATE decimal walks i past the key buffer into adjacent heap memory (CWE-125).

Reproduce
The decimal extension is compiled into the project sqlite3, so the decimal collation resolves without .load. The db is built by the SQL itself. A tiny page cache plus many wide rows force the external merge sort, whose PMA reader allocates each record into a tight unpadded buffer, and an all-whitespace sort key under COLLATE decimal then reads off the end of it.

