Received in a private email from Mohammad Hossein Abedini

Hi,

I found an integer overflow in SQLite's session rebaser that leads to
a heap buffer overflow. In ext/session/sqlite3session.c, the size
calculation for a rebase buffer multiplies two values derived from the
input before passing the result to malloc. With sufficiently large
inputs the multiplication wraps a 32-bit integer, allocating an
undersized buffer while the write assumes the full computed size.

Full analysis and reproducer below.

Vulnerability Details
Bug 1: sessionAppendRecordMerge (line 6884)
File: sqlite3session.c, line 6884
static void sessionAppendRecordMerge(
SessionBuffer *pBuf, int nCol,
u8 *a1, int n1,    /* size of first changeset record — up to ~2GB */
u8 *a2, int n2,    /* size of second changeset record — up to ~2GB */
int *pRc
){
sessionBufferGrow(pBuf, n1+n2, pRc);   /* LINE 6884: int arithmetic
— OVERFLOWS */
if( *pRc==SQLITE_OK ){
...
for(i=0; i<nCol; i++){
int nn2 = sessionSerialLen(a2);    /* up to ~1GB for BLOB column */
...
memcpy(pOut, a2, nn2);            /* WRITES ~1GB into
under-allocated buffer */
pOut += nn2;
}
}
}

Overflow mechanics:

SESSION_MAX_BUFFER_SZ = 0x7FFFFF00 - 1 ≈ 2,147,483,135 (individual
record max)
With n1 = 1,073,741,830 and n2 = 1,073,741,830: n1 + n2 =
2,147,483,660 → wraps to -2,147,483,636 in int
Passed to sessionBufferGrow(pBuf, -2147483636, pRc): nReq =
pBuf->nBuf + (i64)(-2147483636) is deeply negative → nReq >
pBuf->nAlloc is false → no allocation → returns SQLITE_OK
Per-column loop writes sessionSerialLen(a2) ≈ 1GB bytes past buffer end

Bug 2: sessionAppendPartialUpdate (line 6933)
File: sqlite3session.c, line 6933
sessionBufferGrow(pBuf, 2+nRec+nChange, pRc);

Same root cause: 2 + nRec + nChange overflows int when nRec ≈
1GB and nChange ≈ 1GB.
Triggers on pIter->op == SQLITE_UPDATE + pChange->op ==
SQLITE_INSERT branch.

Call Paths
Bug 1 Trigger (UPDATE into DELETE)sqlite3rebaser_configure(p, nRebase1, pRebase1)
→ sessionChangesetToHash → sessionOneChangeToHash
→ sessionChangeMerge → SessionChange stored with nRecord ≈ 1GB

sqlite3rebaser_rebase(p, nIn2, pIn2, ...)     // UPDATE changeset, same PK
→ sessionRebase:
sessionSkipRecord(&pCsr, nCol)
sessionAppendRecordMerge(&sOut, nCol,
pCsr,              nRec-(pCsr-aRec),  // n1 ≈ 1GB
pChange->aRecord,  pChange->nRecord,  // n2 ≈ 1GB (DELETE record)
&rc)                                  // → OVERFLOW at line 6884

Trigger conditions: pIter->op == SQLITE_UPDATE and pChange->op ==
SQLITE_DELETE (line 7059).

Bug 2 Trigger (DELETE into INSERT)
Same sessionRebase call path with pIter->op == SQLITE_DELETE,
pChange->op == SQLITE_INSERT (line 7083).

