Summary
A bare column referenced through t1 FULL JOIN t2 USING(x) is rewritten by lookupName() (src/resolve.c) into a synthetic coalesce(t1.x, t2.x, ...) whose argument list is pFJMatch. At the authorization site the code sets pExpr = pFJMatch->a[0].pExpr (resolve.c:846) and issues a single sqlite3AuthRead() (resolve.c:849), so only the head table's column is authorized; the other join columns pFJMatch->a[1..] are read and materialized at run time but never pass through the authorizer (CWE-863). Because lookupName() returns WRC_Prune, the tree walker never descends into the remaining coalesce arguments to authorize them.

Reproduce
Schema: t1(x) holds only x=1; t2(x,y2) holds the protected x=99. Using the shell's .auth ON (shellAuth prints every SQLITE_READ callback):
CREATE TABLE t1(x,y1); INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(1,'a');
CREATE TABLE t2(x,y2); INSERT INTO t2 VALUES(99,'z');
.auth ON
SELECT x FROM t2;                              -- baseline: emits READ "t2" "x"
SELECT x,y2 FROM t1 FULL JOIN t2 USING(x);     -- exploit
=== BASELINE ===
authorizer: READ "t2" "x" "main" NULL
99
=== EXPLOIT (FULL JOIN USING(x)) ===
authorizer: READ "t1" "x" "main" NULL
authorizer: READ "t2" "y2" "main" NULL      <- NO "READ t2 x" callback
1|
99|z                                         <- x=99 exists only in t2.x, yet returned

Fix/* src/resolve.c lookupName(): authorize every FULL JOIN USING branch. */
if( pFJMatch ){
int ii;
for(ii=0; ii<pFJMatch->nExpr; ii++){
Expr *pE = pFJMatch->a[ii].pExpr;
if( pE->op==TK_COLUMN || pE->op==TK_TRIGGER ){
sqlite3AuthRead(pParse, pE, pSchema, pNC->pSrcList);
}
}
}else if( pExpr->op==TK_COLUMN || pExpr->op==TK_TRIGGER ){
sqlite3AuthRead(pParse, pExpr, pSchema, pNC->pSrcList);
}

That check-in does not change the observable behavior. The authorizer still never sees any USING term except the first, so the bypass ylwang reported is still present at trunk tip today (checked against 7bc7e25cc7c2e98d8aa50dda0db2e9c502be95a3 and current master). There is also a released-version exposure noted below that may not be tracked.

1. The loop indexes a[0] rather than a[ii]
src/resolve.c, lookupName():

for(ii=0; ii<pFJMatch->nExpr; ii++){
assert( pFJMatch->a[0].pExpr->op==TK_COLUMN );
sqlite3AuthRead(pParse, pFJMatch->a[0].pExpr, pSchema, pNC->pSrcList);
}

ii is the loop variable but both lines index element 0. Element 0 is authorized nExpr times; elements 1 through nExpr-1 are never submitted. The net effect matches the pre-check-in code, with only the callback count changed.

Suggested fix:

for(ii=0; ii<pFJMatch->nExpr; ii++){
assert( pFJMatch->a[ii].pExpr->op==TK_COLUMN );
sqlite3AuthRead(pParse, pFJMatch->a[ii].pExpr, pSchema, pNC->pSrcList);
}

