Hello,

While packaging sqlite3 3.53.3 for build2 I encountered that the following
command crashes on Windows:

sqlite3.exe f.sqlar -Ac f.txt

The reason for that is that the free() function call in the following code (shell.c)
refers inside an allocated area:
int SQLITE_CDECL wmain(int argc, wchar_t **wargv){
{
...

rc = utf8_main(argc, argv);
for(i=0; i<argc; i++) free(orig[i]);

...
}

That happens because the utf8_main() call in the previous line "spoils" the argument address in the
argv[i] = &z[2]; line of the following code (shell.c):
int SQLITE_CDECL main(int argc, char **argv){
...
open_db(&data, OPEN_DB_ZIPFILE);
if( z[2] ){
argv[i] = &z[2];
arDotCommand(&data, 1, argv+(i-1), argc-(i-1));
}else{
arDotCommand(&data, 1, argv+i, argc-i);
}
...
}

The issue can be fixed by changing the above code as follows:
int SQLITE_CDECL main(int argc, char **argv){
...
open_db(&data, OPEN_DB_ZIPFILE);
if( z[2] ){
+       char *tmp = argv[i];
argv[i] = &z[2];
arDotCommand(&data, 1, argv+(i-1), argc-(i-1));
+       argv[i] = tmp;
}else{
arDotCommand(&data, 1, argv+i, argc-i);
}
...
}

