Summary
In ext/misc/spellfix.c, editDist3Install() (line 1210) registers the editdist3 SQL function three times under different argument counts, all three sharing one heap-allocated EditDist3Config *pConfig as the pApp context pointer:
static int editDist3Install(sqlite3 *db){
int rc;
EditDist3Config *pConfig = sqlite3_malloc64( sizeof(*pConfig) );
if( pConfig==0 ) return SQLITE_NOMEM;
memset(pConfig, 0, sizeof(*pConfig));
rc = sqlite3_create_function_v2(db, "editdist3",
2, SQLITE_UTF8|SQLITE_DETERMINISTIC, pConfig,
editDist3SqlFunc, 0, 0, 0);                          /* line 1215, xDestroy = 0 */
if( rc==SQLITE_OK ){
rc = sqlite3_create_function_v2(db, "editdist3",
3, SQLITE_UTF8|SQLITE_DETERMINISTIC, pConfig,
editDist3SqlFunc, 0, 0, 0);                         /* line 1219, xDestroy = 0 */
}
if( rc==SQLITE_OK ){
rc = sqlite3_create_function_v2(db, "editdist3",
1, SQLITE_UTF8|SQLITE_DETERMINISTIC, pConfig,
editDist3SqlFunc, 0, 0, editDist3ConfigDelete);     /* line 1224, only this one frees pConfig */
}else{
sqlite3_free(pConfig);                                         /* line 1228 */
}
return rc;
}

Only the third (nArg=1) registration is given editDist3ConfigDelete as its xDestroy — deliberately, since attaching the same destructor to all three registrations would free pConfig three times when the connection closes. But the else at line 1228 fires whenever rc!=SQLITE_OK at that point in the function, which covers three distinct predecessor states, not just "nothing registered yet":

The nArg=2 call itself failed — nothing registered, safe to free.
The nArg=2 call succeeded but the nArg=3 call failed — editdist3/2 is now live in the schema with pApp=pConfig, xDestroy=0, and the else branch frees pConfig out from under it.
Both nArg=2 and nArg=3 succeeded but nArg=1 failed — same problem, now with two dangling live registrations.

In cases 2 and 3, any subsequent call to editdist3(...) reaches editDist3SqlFunc() (line ~1170), which does EditDist3Config *pConfig = (EditDist3Config*)sqlite3_user_data(context); and dereferences it directly (editDist3FindLang(pConfig, iLang), editDist3ConfigLoad(pConfig, db, zTable)), producing a heap-use-after-free.

Reaching case 2/3 requires sqlite3_create_function_v2() to fail immediately after an identical call with the same shared pApp just succeeded — realistically only via a memory allocation failure injected into SQLite's internal function-registration path (the same class of OOM-injection PoC already used in this report for Vuln55/Vuln56). This bug is present unmodified in SQLite's public GitHub trunk as of commit 701092f4a5e8320460219dab733f31dc7a723629 (2026-07-25) — confirmed by fetching and diffing against that commit directly; the local audit checkout (e087d0f, 2026-05-18) has byte-identical code at this location.

Reproduce
A custom SQLITE_CONFIG_MALLOC mock allocator (oom_mock_static.c) is used to fail exactly one allocation of a chosen size, following the same technique as Vuln55/Vuln56. Default per-connection lookaside must be disabled globally (sqlite3_config(SQLITE_CONFIG_LOOKASIDE, 0, 0)) before sqlite3_open(), otherwise SQLite intercepts small allocations (including the internal FuncDef struct for "editdist3", 88 bytes here) via lookaside before they ever reach the configured allocator. The mock is armed to let the first 88-byte allocation succeed (the nArg=2 registration) and fail the second (the nArg=3 registration).

Build against SQLite trunk commit 701092f4a5e8320460219dab733f31dc7a723629:
gcc -g -O0 -fsanitize=address -DSQLITE_CORE -DSQLITE_ENABLE_LOAD_EXTENSION \
-DSQLITE_EXTRA_INIT=oom_extra_init -I. \
-o sqlite3_static_shell shell.c sqlite3.c ext/misc/spellfix.c oom_mock_static.c \
-ldl -lpthread -lm

oom_mock_static.c installs the mock allocator via a SQLITE_CONFIG_MALLOC hook and registers two helper SQL functions through SQLITE_EXTRA_INIT: oom_arm(minSize, maxSize, skipCount) arms the fail-window, and spellfix_install() calls sqlite3_spellfix_init() on the current connection so the OOM window can be armed from inside a running shell session.

SQL script (poc2_static.sql):
SELECT oom_arm(88, 88, 1);       -- let the 1st 88-byte alloc through, fail the 2nd
SELECT spellfix_install();       -- triggers editDist3Install(): nArg=2 succeeds, nArg=3 OOMs, pConfig freed
SELECT oom_arm(999999999, 0, 0); -- disarm, so the query below allocates normally
SELECT editdist3('kitten','sitting');   -- editdist3/2 still registered, pApp now dangling

Run:
ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0 ./sqlite3_static_shell :memory: < poc2_static.sql

