Summary
The zipfile virtual table's xRollback method (zipfileRollback in ext/misc/zipfile.c) is implemented as a direct call to zipfileCommit rather than discarding the in-memory pending entries and truncating the file back to its original size. As a result, any INSERT performed inside a transaction that is later rolled back is written to the underlying zip archive on disk exactly as if it had been committed.

CWE: CWE-460. Severity: Medium.

PoCCREATE VIRTUAL TABLE t1 USING zipfile('verify_rb.zip');
