sha1QueryFunc hashes each BLOB column of an inner query by reading n2 from sqlite3_column_bytes() and z2 from sqlite3_column_blob(), then calling hash_step(&cx, z2, n2) with no NULL check. sqlite3ValueBytes() reports the logical size of a MEM_Zero value (p->n + p->u.nZero) without materializing the bytes. sqlite3_value_blob() then runs ExpandBlob / sqlite3VdbeMemExpandBlob(), which allocates that many bytes; on allocation failure it returns NULL while n2 remains positive. hash_step copies len bytes from data, so a NULL pointer with a positive length reaches memcpy.

With the sha1 extension and PRAGMA hard_heap_limit=2097152, SELECT sha1_query('SELECT zeroblob(n) FROM (SELECT 3000000 AS n)') prepares a non-constant zeroblob so the result stays an unexpanded MEM_Zero blob through sqlite3_step. Dispatch reaches sha1QueryFunc, which takes the SQLITE_BLOB branch and aborts in hash_step.

