fts5DlidxIterInit() loads FTS5_DLIDX_ROWID(segid, height, leaf) records from %_data and increments pIter->nLvl until a node whose first byte has bit 0 clear. The format comment documents a 32-level height, but the loop does not enforce it. fts5DlidxIterNextR() and fts5DlidxIterPrevR() then recurse once per stored level.

In the following PoC, a writable-schema update plants extra internal %_data rows on a real FTS5 table. MATCH 'a AND x' seeks through fts5SegIterNextFrom(): the default rowid order calls fts5DlidxIterNext → fts5DlidxIterNextR; ORDER BY rowid DESC calls fts5DlidxIterPrev → fts5DlidxIterPrevR.

