qpvtabStrAppendValue copies a TEXT constraint into the planner idxStr using sqlite3_value_bytes(), so an embedded NUL is preserved. qpvtabFilter then sets pCur->nData from strlen(idxStr), which stops at that NUL. The aConstraint record therefore has no visible '\n'. qpvtabNext does strchr(z, '\n'), gets NULL, skips the zEnd++ increment, and stores (int)(zEnd - pCur->zData) in iRowid. qpvtabEof and qpvtabColumn only test iRowid < nData, so a negative offset is treated as an in-range row and &pCur->zData[pCur->iRowid] reads before the buffer.

A query of the form SELECT rowid, vn FROM qpvtab WHERE a = CAST(x'610062' AS TEXT) loads the qpvtab module, plans through qpvtabBestIndex → qpvtabStrAppendValue, rewinds with qpvtabFilter, then walks rows via qpvtabNext / qpvtabEof / qpvtabColumn / qpvtabRowid. After the truncated constraint row, the next column fetch uses the invalid iRowid.

Reproduction
Requires the qpvtab extension built from 3.53.4 ext/misc/qpvtab.c (sqlite-extensions-3.53.4/qpvtab.so). No extra CLI flags.
.load qpvtab
SELECT rowid, vn FROM qpvtab WHERE a = CAST(x'610062' AS TEXT);

