vtablogQuote prints an sqlite3_value as an SQL literal. In the SQLITE_BLOB branch it stores n = sqlite3_value_bytes(p) and then z = sqlite3_value_blob(p), and it walks z[i] for i < n with no null check. sqlite3_value_bytes() reports the size of a MEM_Zero zeroblob without materializing it (p->n + p->u.nZero). sqlite3_value_blob() then calls ExpandBlob / sqlite3VdbeMemExpandBlob, which allocates that full size. When that allocation fails, sqlite3_value_blob returns NULL while n is still positive, and the loop dereferences z[i].

The path is an INSERT of a large zeroblob into a vtablog virtual table after PRAGMA hard_heap_limit is set below the expansion size. SQLite dispatches xUpdate to vtablogUpdate, which calls vtablogQuote on each argv[i].

